{"id": "EUVD-2026-80474", "enisaUuid": "e830cc51-afde-39c6-9963-65242fdb18de", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: v4l2-async: avoid deleting unlinked ASC entry on link error\n\nv4l2_async_match_notify() creates ancillary media links before adding\nasc->asc_subdev_entry to sd->asc_list.\n\nIf ancillary link creation fails, the function jumps to\nerr_call_unbind while asc_subdev_entry has not been linked yet. Async\nconnections are zero-allocated, so the list entry still has NULL next\nand prev pointers on this path. Calling list_del() on it can therefore\ndereference NULL instead of returning the original link creation error.\n\nDo not delete asc_subdev_entry from err_call_unbind. There is no list\ninsertion to undo on this path; the bound callback and sub-device\nregistration are the operations that need to be rolled back.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d273571e531405426983c6a45ec635c7d0415eed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/caac13f518d83974e9884d1eeda3d4cc3bb92978", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3345746e0957bce6c53644838e4955710a82a962", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a57d94026cb4fd7b3d258f0db2ad391cbccfaba5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47d82b605351c0e04f6365e42c8ffe2fcfdba615"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rmqv-gxqc-vfx4", "CVE-2026-89874"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "242ef06d-28f0-3b37-a911-cde57de9f2b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "28a1295795d85a25f2e7dd391c43969e95fcb341 <a57d94026cb4fd7b3d258f0db2ad391cbccfaba5"}, {"id": "4022ce2f-b427-349d-991f-25f387847786", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "50972e1a-edb3-3caa-99ed-04aea08d01f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "67d01f85-a196-30f1-a4a3-7c66466485b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "28a1295795d85a25f2e7dd391c43969e95fcb341 <caac13f518d83974e9884d1eeda3d4cc3bb92978"}, {"id": "7280371d-44e4-3e97-8a23-2a3c2957e347", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "28a1295795d85a25f2e7dd391c43969e95fcb341 <d273571e531405426983c6a45ec635c7d0415eed"}, {"id": "8ade7105-7b00-3968-a53b-d9d1b7eb4cd0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "a3d4c0f0-204e-3b9e-875f-0b74dbbd0faf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "b3fab65f-5455-3f48-8113-a64334739d97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "c4b4b92b-fb08-319d-989f-8453e8275591", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "28a1295795d85a25f2e7dd391c43969e95fcb341 <3345746e0957bce6c53644838e4955710a82a962"}, {"id": "ce0e48df-53aa-3f9c-8c46-8f2158d095a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "e89056b7-78dd-3cf1-9c41-703e28bf737e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "28a1295795d85a25f2e7dd391c43969e95fcb341 <47d82b605351c0e04f6365e42c8ffe2fcfdba615"}, {"id": "f71a44ca-a559-3803-9a6d-20dd18e2d129", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4d2d714e-4c32-3767-805b-60d14322e26b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}